WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.468
Step two.

00:00:00.518 --> 00:00:04.782
Before we deploy anything, we make sure the subscription is ready: resource

00:00:04.832 --> 00:00:08.579
providers, v CPU quota, and a resource group in Indonesia Central.

00:00:08.629 --> 00:00:10.713
In the Azure portal, open Subscriptions,

00:00:10.763 --> 00:00:13.542
and select the subscription you'll use for this demo.

00:00:13.592 --> 00:00:17.832
In the subscription menu, search for resource providers, and open that page.

00:00:17.882 --> 00:00:18.847
Filter by name.

00:00:18.897 --> 00:00:23.719
Microsoft dot Container Service, the AKS provider, must show Registered.

00:00:23.769 --> 00:00:28.413
Microsoft dot Monitor powers the Azure Monitor workspace for managed Prometheus.

00:00:28.463 --> 00:00:29.586
It's registered too.

00:00:29.636 --> 00:00:33.312
Microsoft dot Policy Insights is used by the Azure Policy add-on.

00:00:33.362 --> 00:00:37.094
If a provider shows Not Registered, select it and choose Register.

00:00:37.144 --> 00:00:37.838
Next, quota.

00:00:37.888 --> 00:00:40.318
Open Quotas, then My quotas for Compute,

00:00:40.368 --> 00:00:43.231
and set the region filter to Indonesia Central.

00:00:43.281 --> 00:00:44.894
Search for DDS version 5.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:50.480
The cluster needs eight v CP Us for two nodes, and sixteen if it scales out to four.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:55.342
Now open Resource groups, and select Create.

00:00:55.392 --> 00:00:59.214
Keep your subscription, name the group RG contoso health AKS,

00:00:59.264 --> 00:01:00.801
and open the region list.

00:01:00.851 --> 00:01:04.645
Choose Indonesia Central, so data and compute stay in Indonesia.

00:01:04.695 --> 00:01:05.700
Open the Tags tab.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:09.161
Tags drive cost reporting, and they make ownership obvious.

00:01:09.211 --> 00:01:13.053
Add three tags: workload, environment, and cost center.

00:01:13.103 --> 00:01:15.176
Then select Review and create.

00:01:15.226 --> 00:01:17.357
Check the summary, and select Create.

00:01:17.407 --> 00:01:17.639
Done.

00:01:17.689 --> 00:01:20.912
Everything for this demo lands in this one resource group,

00:01:20.962 --> 00:01:23.000
so clean-up later is a single delete.
